        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "84170444-4640-546e-9284-2559fc2d59a3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Cymbidium, Patrinia, Thelymitra\n- Places: China, Siberia, Japan, Sessa Orchid Sanctuary\n- Organizations/Systems: Orchidaceae\n- Products/Projects: Cymbidium hybrids, cut-flower production\n\nFacts:\n- Cymbidium, also called boat orchid, is a genus of 52 evergreen species in the orchid family Orchidaceae.\n- Patrinia includes about 17 species native to grassy mountain habitats in China, Siberia, and Japan.\n- Thelymitra, commonly known as sun orchids, is a genus of more than 100 species in the orchid family Orchidaceae.\n- Sessa Orchid Sanctuary has a nursery with representative specimens of various orchid species from the sanctuary and a demonstration farm of Cymbidium hybrids for cut-flower production.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "21c3718a-a0a5-5058-9e87-174cb781c639",
        "text": "Page: Cymbidium. Sentence: Cymbidium , or boat orchid, is a genus of 52 evergreen species in the orchid family Orchidaceae.\nPage: Patrinia. Sentence: There are about 17 species native to grassy mountain habitats in China, Siberia and Japan.\nPage: Sessa Orchid Sanctuary. Sentence: A nursery includes representative specimens of various orchid species of the sanctuary and a demonstration farm of Cymbidium hybrids for cut-flower production.\nPage: Thelymitra. Sentence: Thelymitra, commonly known as sun orchids, is a genus of more than 100 species of plants in the orchid family, Orchidaceae.",
